## Brute-Force Protection

Use Upstash Redis.

Requirement:

Five consecutive failed login attempts must trigger a 15-minute lockout.

Implement:
- IP-based rate limiting.
- Normalized account-based failure tracking.
- Atomic Redis operations.
- Lock expiration.
- Successful-login counter reset.
- Proper generic error messages.

Do not expose whether an email address exists.

The lockout must be enforced server-side, not only through disabled frontend buttons.

# 8. FORGOT PASSWORD AND OTP

Implement a three-step recovery experience.

Page 1: /forgot-password

- Work Email.
- Validate email.
- Request six-digit OTP through Supabase Auth.
- Show confirmation message.

Rate limiting:

- Maximum three OTP resend requests per 15 minutes.
- Upstash Redis.
- Separate email and IP protection.
- 60-second resend cooldown.

Page 2: /verify-otp

Create six individual input fields.

Requirements:
- Numeric input.
- Auto-focus.
- Backspace navigation.
- Paste support.
- Auto-submit when all digits are entered.
- 60-second resend timer.
